this is the moment isil detainees  escaped from prison in northern syria  for four days isil fighters have  attempted to free their fellow members  it's unclear how many have managed to  escape  how many have been killed or recaptured  by kurdish forces who are being  supported by u.s airstrikes the prison  houses more than 1 200 prisoners from 50  different nationalities  it's seen as the most significant attack  by isil since the armed group was  defeated in the region three years ago  this footage shows isil fighters  breaking into prison  a pile of bodies dressed in uniform lay  in the corner  kurdish forces say they have the upper  hand  now daesh exists only in the prison i  mean apart from the prison they don't  exist anywhere so they are controlling  the prison only and we are surrounding  them  they do have weapons i don't deny that  but they can't do anything with that  they might run out of ammunition and  therefore they don't fight back  residents near the prison are fleeing  the fighting  there's been bombing war pains and  conflicts since yesterday and young  people were slaughtered what is  happening the situation is catastrophic  we fled the shelling in conflict we got  scared for our children and fled  there's also reports isil fighters have  broken into homes and killed people  they're slaughtering  members broken and killed four men our  neighbors two of them were brothers  [Music]  as the fighting continues the fear now  is whether this attack means a  significant return by the armed group or  a one-off attempt to replenish its  numbers for a future front against  kurdish forces assalbaig al-jazeera
 

